From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 04:49:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Optionally retire a lone render
 without cached CONTEXT

g16_lone_ctx_skip=1 (run time, default 0) acts only with
g16_notifier_cached=1. Then the proof of a render with nothing
published behind it no longer needs the TA and FS record CONTEXT words,
the one host read of the ASC-cached record page. The firmware stores
them there at every TA and FS post, and they reach memory only when it
cleans that line, so the host may read an older value. The uncached
firmware and service stamps, both queue receipts, the pool and the
scene timestamps still prove the render, as they already prove a render
with work behind it, whose proof never reads CONTEXT.

With g16_notifier_cached=1 every lone proof pass that every uncached
witness passed is counted by its CONTEXT words in the stats line
"lone_ctx: skip S matched M held H skipped K": matched, held back
(word 0), or retired without them (word 1). The rule is the pure
function in lone_ctx.rs. Without g16_notifier_cached the proof is the
old expression, unchanged.

This is the release-line port of the experimental-line change. On this
line the render pool witness is pool_retired(k), which both branches
keep.

Assisted-by: LLM
